From 58bef2e7255b39667f34665217a7b6b6e2aa7213 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick McMillen <153555205+nmcmil@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 02:42:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: isolate fixture startup and begin Wi-Fi page
 composition

Compose the initial Wi-Fi, connection, known-network and hotspot views from the C LumaUI card and type APIs. Keep this partial view separate from live service adapters and reject pages which are not ported yet. Use an isolated application ID and force the memory settings backend before startup; never instantiate the GNOME panel loader in fixture mode. Exercise widget-driven radio dependencies, independent fixture copies and queued redraw destruction in a private display.
---
